Negative control for the page's content column NOT exporting its own content
width to the document (T2.5 · `AC2.4` · `P1-R5`).

The column is a flex ITEM of the layout's one row — the sidebar beside it — so it
defaults to `min-width:auto` and refuses to be laid out narrower than its own
content. Anything inside it that cannot shrink therefore stops being an overflow
INSIDE the page and becomes the page's own width: the sidebar is squeezed past
its declared `w-64`, the document grows, and every viewport under the content's
minimum gets a horizontal scrollbar. Measured at 1280 with a force preset armed,
the scenario bar's picker naming the armed preset was enough — `scrollWidth`
1289 / 1349 / 1379 against a 1280 client width, the badge, Add new and the
Scenario toggle all clipped off-screen.

`min-w-0` is the floor that makes the column shrink to its share and lets the
row inside it truncate, which is what the bar's own playlist is built to do. It
takes NO width from the page in any state, open sheet or closed, so it is not
the `P1-R5` compensation the sibling control pins — that mutant adds width, this
one removes the floor.

This mutant is the removal alone: the column, the sidebar, the header, the sheet
host and every treatment on them are untouched.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the T2.5 case asserting the layout's content column declares a zero
min-width floor. It cannot be caught by anything that mounts the layout: jsdom
computes no layout, so the squeeze, the sidebar and the document width are all
invisible there — which is exactly why the claim is read off the layout SOURCE,
the way the `P1-R5` compensation claim beside it already is. A browser-lane
read-back of `document.scrollWidth` at 1280 under each force preset is the
stronger proof and belongs to the e2e lane.

  Proven RED: owed by the prover's blind run (`vitest run default-layout`).
  Recorded here rather than pre-filled — the seat that authors the mutant is not
  the seat that grades it.

